schema_version: '1.0'
action: repair
root_cause: "The RTL's AES-128 datapath is functionally corrupted. Multiple\
  \ independent RTL defects jointly corrupt the ciphertext\
  \ of every transaction: (1) 10 SBOX entries differ from FIPS-197; (2) RCON has wrong\
  \ values (0x03, 0x81) and is declared [1:10] while indexed with round 0..9 (RCON[0]\
  \ out-of-bounds / off-by-one Rcon); (3) gm2 reduces with 8'h1d instead of 8'h1b;\
  \ (4) gm3 = gm2(a)^gm2(a) so gm3\u22610; (5) mix_columns uses wrong/swapped xtime-2/xtime-3\
  \ coefficients (incl. gm3 on b[4c+3]); (6) shift_rows mis-maps 5 byte lanes; (7)\
  \ next_round_key slices words at k[126:95]/k[94:63]/k[62:31]/k[30:0], swaps the\
  \ two RotWord bytes, and chains n1=w1^w0, n3=w3^n1; (8) aes_round applies MixColumns\
  \ only in the final round on the pre-round state, omits it for non-final rounds,\
  \ and XORs ~k instead of k; (9) the control FSM loads round_key <= ~key on start\
  \ and the round==9 state update uses the previous round key (K9) instead of the\
  \ next round key (K10). Net effect: known-answer, corner, and randomized transactions\
  \ all emit wrong ciphertext (FIPS-197 vector: 0x31de... instead of 0x69c4...)."
evidence:
- 'Frozen cocotb/pyuvm results (tb/.chia_sim/*.xml) show functional ciphertext mismatches
  against the spec/reference model: TC01/TC02/TC05/TC09 FIPS-197 vector expected 0x69c4e0d86a7b0430d8cdb78070b4c55a,
  got 0x31de36532b58fd22ec1cc2c6a3794f5e; TC03 all-zero expected 0x66e94bd4ef8a2c3b884cfa59ca342b2e,
  got 0xd9f2b607052c98bf25693d0d5abc1069; TC04 incrementing expected 0x0a940bb5416ef045f1c39458c653ea5a,
  got 0x63d554b5894a82b57a3b6aba5581f0c1; all-ones corner expected 0xbcbf217cb280cf30b2517052193ab979,
  got 0x2531b8823221b92e98692c7f189c2226; key/plaintext sensitivity, determinism and
  randomized scenarios fail the ''ciphertext_matches_reference'' assertion. No timeouts/watchdogs
  or X-states are reported, so this is an RTL functional defect, not a TB/toolchain
  fault.'
- An exact Python re-simulation of the RTL as written (replicating its SBOX, RCON,
  gm2=0x1d, gm3=0, shift_rows indices, mix_columns coefficients, key expansion, ~k
  rounds, and control flow) reproduces every reported wrong ciphertext byte-for-byte
  (31de..., d9f2..., 63d5..., 2531...), proving the observed failures are generated
  by this RTL.
- Applying the listed repairs to the re-simulation makes the RTL logic match the reference
  model on all three KAT vectors, the all-ones corner vector, and 20 randomized inputs
  (reference_model.py self-check passes), confirming the spec/reference model (not
  the current RTL) defines intended behavior and that the repair set is exactly sufficient.
