  - 'shift_rows (lines 76-79): correct the byte-lane indices: o[1]=b[5], o[6]=b[14],
    o[11]=b[7], o[12]=b[12], o[15]=b[11] (keep o[0]=b[0], o[2]=b[10], o[3]=b[15],
    o[4]=b[4], o[5]=b[9], o[7]=b[3], o[8]=b[8], o[9]=b[13], o[10]=b[2], o[13]=b[1],
    o[14]=b[6]).'
  - 'mix_columns (lines 96-99): use the correct FIPS-197 coefficients: o[4*c+0] =
    gm2(b[4*c+0]) ^ gm3(b[4*c+1]) ^ b[4*c+2] ^ b[4*c+3]; o[4*c+1] = b[4*c+0] ^ gm2(b[4*c+1])
    ^ gm3(b[4*c+2]) ^ b[4*c+3]; o[4*c+2] = b[4*c+0] ^ b[4*c+1] ^ gm2(b[4*c+2]) ^ gm3(b[4*c+3]);
    o[4*c+3] = gm3(b[4*c+0]) ^ b[4*c+1] ^ b[4*c+2] ^ gm2(b[4*c+3]).'
  - 'next_round_key (lines 111-124): slice the current round key as w0=k[127:96],
    w1=k[95:64], w2=k[63:32], w3=k[31:0]; build the RotWord+SubWord word as t = {SBOX[w3[23:16]],
    SBOX[w3[15:8]], SBOX[w3[7:0]], SBOX[w3[31:24]]}; apply the Rcon as t[31:24] =
    t[31:24] ^ RCON[r] (drop the spurious ''^ 32''h00000100''); and chain the round-key
    words as n1 = w1 ^ n0, n3 = w3 ^ n2 (n0 = w0 ^ t, n2 = w2 ^ n1 unchanged).'
  - 'aes_round (lines 135-140): match FIPS-197 round semantics: after shift_rows/sub_bytes
    apply MixColumns only for non-final rounds and on the transformed state (''if
    (!final_round) t = mix_columns(t);''), and return ''t ^ k'' instead of ''t ^ ~k''.'
  - 'Control FSM (lines 154, 162-164): on start capture ''round_key <= key'' instead
    of ''round_key <= ~key'', and in the round==4''d9 completion branch drive both
    state and ciphertext from the next round key: ''state <= aes_round(state, next_round_key(round_key,
    round), 1''b1)'' (same expression as the ciphertext assignment) so the 10th round
    uses K10 rather than the stale round_key (K9). (ciphertext assignment already
    uses next_round_key(...); state must match.) No other changes are required.'

